# {{1811}} A [[cuckold]], from the horns planted on the head of Acteon by Diana. (1811 ''Dictionary of Vulgar Tongue'')

====Quotations====
* '''1819''', ''The Hermit in London'', published in ''The Literary Gazette and Journal of Belles Lettres'', Number 126, on Saturday, June 19, 1819, and reprinted in the compilation of Gazette issues printed at the end of that year by William Pople: <!-- page 397 of the compilation -->
*: He once lost a friend by kindly inquiring after his wife, who had made an '''Acteon''' of him, first by the head ornament presented, and secondly by sending him to the dogs in the way of pecuniary circumstances.

